IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-nouns`
IMPORT `g6-notice-and-hearing`

-- g6-appeal-and-publication.l4: ss.55-57.  One sanction for one act (s.55), the appeal to the Magistrates' Court
-- within 45 days, the stay and the refund with shekel interest (s.56), and publication on the Ministry's website
-- with its limits and its duration (s.57).
--
-- Clock convention for the regulative rules here: `AT 0` is the day the period runs from (the day notice of the
-- decision was delivered; the day of publication); an event `AT k` happened k days after it.
--
-- Periods owned here (PLAN section (d)):
--   P35, s.56(a): 45 days from the day notice of the decision was delivered: a window in which an appeal may be
--     brought, kind W.  IL s.10(a); IL s.10(c) applied (ruling 4); the alternative without it is callable.
--   P36, s.56(c): "from the day of payment until the day of its return": a stretch of days, kind V; the shekel
--     interest over it is an input.
--   P37, s.57(e): four years (a corporation) or two years (an individual) of publication: a period of validity,
--     kind V: IL s.10(b), years after an event, and IL s.10(c) NOT applied (ruling 4); the alternative that applies
--     it is callable.
--
-- Not in the sources: which of several breaches by one act carries the single sanction (s.55 leaves it to the
-- Commissioner); the Freedom of Information Law's s.9 (outside the scope); the text of any order under s.57(f).

§ `Chapter 6: administrative enforcement measures`

§§ `Subchapter C: miscellaneous provisions`

§§§ `ss 55 to 57: the nouns and the acts`

@desc One item of the list that s.57(a) requires the Commissioner to publish, with what became of it: published, barred from disclosure under s.9(a) of the Freedom of Information Law, or omitted as s.9(b) allows
DECLARE `Item of a publication under section 57(a)` HAS
    `the item number` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of the item in s.57(a), 1 to 6
    `published` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the item was published on the Ministry website
    `barred from disclosure by section 9(a) of the Freedom of Information Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if a public authority may not disclose the particular under s.9(a) of the Freedom of Information Law
    `omitted because section 9(b) of the Freedom of Information Law does not oblige disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Commissioner chose to leave the item out, the particular being one a public authority need not disclose under s.9(b)

@desc The acts of ss.55 to 57: imposing a second sanction for one act (forbidden), the violator's appeal, publishing the sanction and its appeal, publishing a particular, publishing an individual's name, and the Ministry's blocking of access when the publication period ends, and the Minister's setting of further ways to publish; the first field says who performs each act
DECLARE `Act under ss 55 to 57` IS ONE OF
    `impose a further financial sanction for the same act`
        HAS `performed by the sanctioning officer for one act` IS A Party
    `appeal a final decision of the Commissioner to the Magistrates' Court`
        HAS `performed by the appealing violator` IS A Party
            `lodged with the Magistrates' Court where the President of the Magistrates' Courts sits` IS A BOOLEAN
    `publish on the Ministry website the particulars of the financial sanction`
        HAS `performed by the publishing Commissioner` IS A Party
            `the items published` IS A LIST OF `Item of a publication under section 57(a)`
            `in a way that makes the exercise of the Commissioner's discretion transparent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `publish on the Ministry website that an appeal was filed and how it ended`
        HAS `performed by the Commissioner publishing the appeal` IS A Party
            `states that the appeal was filed` IS A BOOLEAN
            `states the result of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `publish a particular on the Ministry website`
        HAS `performed by the Commissioner publishing a particular` IS A Party
            `the particular` IS AN `Item of a publication under section 57(a)`
    `publish the name of an individual violator on the Ministry website`
        HAS `performed by the Commissioner publishing a name` IS A Party
    `apply technological measures against viewing the published particulars`
        HAS `performed by the Ministry blocking access` IS A Party
    `set further ways of publishing the particulars`
        HAS `performed by the Minister setting further ways` IS A Party

§§§ `s 55: one financial sanction for one act`

-- src:412 | {{ח:סעיף|55|עיצום כספי בשל הפרה לפי חוק זה ולפי חוק אחר}}
-- src:413 | {{ח:ת}} על מעשה אחד המהווה כמה הפרות של הוראות לפי חוק זה המנויות {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 3|בתוספת השלישית}} או של הוראה מההוראות לפי חוק אחר, לא יוטל יותר מעיצום כספי אחד.
-- "For one act that constitutes several breaches of provisions of this Law listed in the Third Schedule, or of a
-- provision of another law, no more than one financial sanction shall be imposed."  The act is identified by
-- `reference for the act` (domain.l4: two violations with the same reference are one act).  A sanction under
-- another law for the same act is a fact (an input).  Which of the several breaches the one sanction is for is
-- the Commissioner's choice (not in the sources, so not decided here).
@ref s.55 (src:413)
GIVEN violation IS A Violation
      `the violations for which a financial sanction was imposed` IS A LIST OF Violation
      `a financial sanction for the same act was imposed under another law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 55 — a financial sanction may still be imposed for` violation `given` `the violations for which a financial sanction was imposed` `and` `a financial sanction for the same act was imposed under another law` MEANS
        "no sanction under another law for the act" ... NOT `a financial sanction for the same act was imposed under another law`
    AND "no sanction under this Law for the act" ... NOT (any (GIVEN other YIELD other's `reference for the act` EQUALS violation's `reference for the act`) `the violations for which a financial sanction was imposed`)

-- The invariant over a list of sanctions imposed: no act has more than one.
@ref s.55 (src:413)
GIVEN `the violations for which a financial sanction was imposed` IS A LIST OF Violation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 55 — no act has more than one financial sanction among` `the violations for which a financial sanction was imposed` MEANS
    all (GIVEN violation YIELD count (filter (GIVEN other YIELD other's `reference for the act` EQUALS violation's `reference for the act`) `the violations for which a financial sanction was imposed`) AT MOST 1) `the violations for which a financial sanction was imposed`

-- The prohibition: once a sanction has been imposed for the act, the Commissioner SHANT impose another.
@ref s.55 (src:413)
GIVEN `a financial sanction has already been imposed for the act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 55 to 57`
`s 55 — the Commissioner shall not impose a further sanction for the same act` `a financial sanction has already been imposed for the act` MEANS
    IF   `a financial sanction has already been imposed for the act`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         SHANT `impose a further financial sanction for the same act` `the Commissioner`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the Commissioner` BECAUSE "s 55: a second financial sanction was imposed for one act"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `s 56: appeal to the Magistrates' Court`

-- src:415 | {{ח:סעיף|56|ערעור}}
-- src:416 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} על החלטה סופית של הממונה לפי {{ח:פנימי|פרק ו|פרק זה}} ניתן לערער לבית משפט השלום שבו יושב נשיא בית משפט השלום, בתוך 45 ימים מיום שנמסרה הודעה על ההחלטה.
-- (a): "A final decision of the Commissioner under this chapter may be appealed to the Magistrates' Court in which
-- the President of the Magistrates' Courts sits, within 45 days of the day notice of the decision was delivered."
-- Kind W: IL s.10(a), the day of delivery not counted, and IL s.10(c) applied.  Trap T39: only the s.56 route is
-- carried; s.62 (the Administrative Courts) is not a fact here.
@ref s.56(a) (src:416)
@export The last day on which a violator may appeal a final decision of the Commissioner to the Magistrates' Court: 45 days from the day notice of the decision was delivered, moved past days of rest, recess or holiday
GIVEN `the day notice of the decision was delivered` IS A DATE @desc The day notice of the Commissioner's final decision was delivered, as an ISO 8601 date
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days` @desc The days of rest, recess or holiday under an enactment for the years the question touches, as a list of dates (never computed)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 56(a) — the last day of the 45 days from` `the day notice of the decision was delivered` `with` calendar MEANS
    `s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 45 `days from` `the day notice of the decision was delivered` `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`Chapter 6 — the days of rest, recess or holiday of` calendar)

@ref s.56(a) (src:416)
GIVEN `the day notice of the decision was delivered` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 56(a) — without s 10(c), the last day of the 45 days from` `the day notice of the decision was delivered` MEANS
    `s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 45 `days from` `the day notice of the decision was delivered`

@ref s.56(a) (src:416)
GIVEN `the day notice of the decision was delivered` IS A DATE
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 56(a) — the days from` `the day notice of the decision was delivered` `to the last day to appeal, with` calendar MEANS
    (Day (`s 56(a) — the last day of the 45 days from` `the day notice of the decision was delivered` `with` calendar)) MINUS (Day `the day notice of the decision was delivered`)

-- Is a day timely, within the s.56 period?  An appeal filed on the day notice of the decision is delivered is "within 45
-- days" of it (fork F-ACTDAY, as at s.43): the day of delivery or later, and the last day or earlier; the last day is
-- inside.
@ref s.56(a) (src:416)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the day notice of the decision was delivered` IS A DATE
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 56(a) — the day` day `is within the period to appeal that runs from` `the day notice of the decision was delivered` `with` calendar MEANS
        (`the day notice of the decision was delivered` AT MOST day)
    AND (day AT MOST `s 56(a) — the last day of the 45 days from` `the day notice of the decision was delivered` `with` calendar)

-- Fork F-ACTDAY: the strict reading, the period beginning the day AFTER the notice of the decision was delivered.
@ref s.56(a) (src:416)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the day notice of the decision was delivered` IS A DATE
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 56(a) — counting the day after delivery as the first day, the day` day `is within the period to appeal that runs from` `the day notice of the decision was delivered` `with` calendar MEANS
    `s 8, s 10 — the date` day `is inside the period beginning on` (`s 10 — the first day of a period counted from or after an event on` `the day notice of the decision was delivered`) `and ending on` (`s 56(a) — the last day of the 45 days from` `the day notice of the decision was delivered` `with` calendar)

-- For a violator who made no representations there is no decision on his case and no notice of one: the notice of
-- intention is treated as a payment demand delivered at the end of the s.43 period (s.44(d)).  Which day is "the day
-- notice of the decision was delivered" for him is not said (fork F-APPEAL-DEEMED): the reading taken is the day the
-- demand is treated as delivered; the alternative is the day the notice of intention was in fact delivered.
@ref s.44(d), s.56(a) (src:416)
GIVEN notice IS A `Notice of intention`
      extension IS A MAYBE `Extension granted by the Commissioner`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 56(a) — the day notice of the decision counts as delivered to a violator who made no representations` notice extension calendar MEANS
    `s 44(d) — the day the notice of intention is treated as a payment demand delivered` notice extension calendar

@ref s.44(d), s.56(a) (src:416)
GIVEN notice IS A `Notice of intention`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 56(a) — the day notice of the decision counts as delivered to a violator who made no representations, taking the day the notice of intention was delivered` notice MEANS
    notice's `delivered on`

-- The right: a violator MAY appeal a final decision of the Commissioner under Chapter 6, lodged in the right court,
-- within the 45 days.
@ref s.56(a) (src:416)
GIVEN `the decision is a final decision of the Commissioner under Chapter 6` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day notice of the decision was delivered` IS A DATE
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 55 to 57`
`s 56(a) — the violator may appeal to the Magistrates' Court` `the decision is a final decision of the Commissioner under Chapter 6` `the day notice of the decision was delivered` calendar MEANS
    IF   `the decision is a final decision of the Commissioner under Chapter 6`
    THEN PARTY  `the violator`
         MAY    `appeal a final decision of the Commissioner to the Magistrates' Court` `the violator` lodgedRight
                PROVIDED lodgedRight
         WITHIN (`s 56(a) — the days from` `the day notice of the decision was delivered` `to the last day to appeal, with` calendar)
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:417 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} אין בהגשת ערעור כאמור בסעיף קטן (א) כדי לעכב את ביצוע ההחלטה, אלא אם כן הסכים לכך הממונה או שבית המשפט הורה על כך.
-- (b): "Filing an appeal does not stay the execution of the decision, unless the Commissioner agreed or the court
-- ordered."
@ref s.56(b) (src:417)
GIVEN `the Commissioner agreed to a stay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court ordered a stay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 56(b) — the filing of the appeal stays the execution of the decision, given` `the Commissioner agreed to a stay` `and` `the court ordered a stay` MEANS
    `the Commissioner agreed to a stay` OR `the court ordered a stay`

-- src:418 | {{ח:תת|(ג)}} החליט בית המשפט, לאחר ששולם העיצום הכספי, לקבל ערעור כאמור בסעיף קטן (א), והורה על החזרת סכום העיצום הכספי ששולם או על הפחתת העיצום הכספי, יוחזר הסכום ששולם או כל חלק ממנו שהופחת, בתוספת ריבית שקלית מיום תשלומו עד יום החזרתו.
-- (c): "If the court decided, after the financial sanction was paid, to accept an appeal and ordered the return of the
-- amount paid or the reduction of the sanction, the amount paid, or any part of it that was reduced, shall be
-- returned, together with shekel interest from the day it was paid until the day of its return."
-- The amount returned is the whole amount paid (the court ordered its return) or the part reduced (the court
-- ordered a reduction to a smaller sanction).  The shekel interest is the Interest and Linkage Law's (outside the
-- scope, no rate in the sources): an input amount, a named refusal when not supplied.  Arrears fees are NOT
-- added to a refund: s.49's two charges are the late payer's, and s.56(c) names only shekel interest (trap T40).
@ref s.56(c) (src:418)
GIVEN `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the sanction as the court reduced it` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 56(c) — the amount to be returned of` `the amount paid` `when the court reduced the sanction to` `the sanction as the court reduced it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the sanction as the court reduced it`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the amount paid`
    WHEN JUST reduced THEN max 0 (`the amount paid` MINUS reduced)

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 56(c) — the shekel interest is fixed by the Interest and Linkage Law, whose rates are not in the sources, and none was supplied` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 56(c) — the shekel interest is fixed by the Interest and Linkage Law, whose rates are not in the sources, and none was supplied"

@ref s.56(c) (src:418)
GIVEN `the amount to be returned` IS A NUMBER
      `the shekel interest accrued from the day of payment to the day of return` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 56(c) — the amount returned with shekel interest` `the amount to be returned` `and` `the shekel interest accrued from the day of payment to the day of return` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the shekel interest accrued from the day of payment to the day of return`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 56(c) — the shekel interest is fixed by the Interest and Linkage Law, whose rates are not in the sources, and none was supplied`
    WHEN JUST interest THEN `the amount to be returned` PLUS interest

-- P36: the stretch of days the interest runs over, from the day of payment until the day of return.
@ref s.56(c) (src:418)
GIVEN `the day of payment` IS A DATE
      `the day of return` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 56(c) — the days from` `the day of payment` `until` `the day of return` MEANS
    max 0 ((Day `the day of return`) MINUS (Day `the day of payment`))

§§§ `s 57: publication`

-- src:420 | {{ח:סעיף|57|פרסום}}
-- src:421 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} הטיל הממונה עיצום כספי לפי {{ח:פנימי|פרק ו|פרק זה}}, יפרסם באתר האינטרנט של המשרד את הפרטים שלהלן, בדרך שתבטיח שקיפות לגבי הפעלת שיקול דעתו בקבלת ההחלטה להטיל עיצום כספי:
-- src:422 | {{ח:תתת|(1)}} דבר הטלת העיצום הכספי;
-- src:423 | {{ח:תתת|(2)}} מהות ההפרה שבשלה הוטל העיצום הכספי, מועד ביצוע ההפרה ונסיבות ההפרה;
-- src:424 | {{ח:תתת|(3)}} סכום העיצום הכספי שהוטל;
-- src:425 | {{ח:תתת|(4)}} אם הופחת סכום העיצום הכספי – הנסיבות שבשלהן הופחת סכום העיצום ושיעורי ההפחתה;
-- src:426 | {{ח:תתת|(5)}} פרטים על אודות המפר, הנוגעים לעניין;
-- src:427 | {{ח:תתת|(6)}} שמו של המפר – אם המפר הוא תאגיד.
-- (a): when the Commissioner imposes a sanction he shall publish on the Ministry's website items (1) to (6), "in a way
-- that ensures transparency regarding the exercise of his discretion".  The items: (1) the fact of imposition, (2) the
-- nature of the breach, its date and its circumstances, (3) the amount, (4) if the amount was reduced, the
-- circumstances and rates of reduction, (5) relevant particulars about the violator, (6) the violator's name, if a
-- corporation.  So items (1), (2), (3) and (5) are always required, (4) only after a reduction, (6) only for a
-- corporation.
@ref s.57(a) (src:421-427)
GIVEN `the amount was reduced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of person` IS A `Person kind`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`s 57(a) — the numbers of the items the Law requires where` `the amount was reduced` `and the violator is` `the kind of person` MEANS
    append (append `items (1), (2) and (3)` `item (4), after a reduction`) (append `item (5)` `item (6), for a corporation`)
    WHERE
        `items (1), (2) and (3)` MEANS LIST 1, 2, 3
        `item (4), after a reduction` MEANS
            IF   `the amount was reduced`
            THEN LIST 4
            ELSE EMPTY
        `item (5)` MEANS LIST 5
        `item (6), for a corporation` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the kind of person`
            WHEN `a corporation` THEN LIST 6
            WHEN `an individual` THEN EMPTY

-- (d), read with (a): an item that s.9(a) of the Freedom of Information Law bars shall NOT be published (so the duty to
-- publish it falls away), and the Commissioner may leave out an item that s.9(b) does not oblige a public authority to
-- disclose.  An item the Law does not require is not a duty either way.
@ref s.57(a), s.57(d) (src:421-430)
GIVEN item IS AN `Item of a publication under section 57(a)`
      `the item is required by section 57(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57(a), (d) — the item is dealt with as the Law requires` item `where it is required:` `the item is required by section 57(a)` MEANS
    IF   item's `barred from disclosure by section 9(a) of the Freedom of Information Law`
    THEN NOT item's `published`
    ELSE IF   `the item is required by section 57(a)`
         THEN item's `published` OR item's `omitted because section 9(b) of the Freedom of Information Law does not oblige disclosure`
         ELSE TRUE

-- Every required number has an item in the list, and every item in the list is dealt with as the Law requires.
@ref s.57(a), s.57(d) (src:421-430)
GIVEN items IS A LIST OF `Item of a publication under section 57(a)`
      `the numbers of the items required` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57(a) — the publication deals with each item as the Law requires, given the items` items `and the numbers required` `the numbers of the items required` MEANS
        "every required item is listed" ... all (GIVEN number YIELD any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number` EQUALS number) items) `the numbers of the items required`
    AND "each item is dealt with as required" ... all (GIVEN item YIELD `s 57(a), (d) — the item is dealt with as the Law requires` item `where it is required:` (elem (item's `the item number`) `the numbers of the items required`)) items

-- The duty: when a sanction is imposed, publish on the Ministry website, in a way that makes the exercise of his
-- discretion transparent.  No time is stated, so no WITHIN.  "In a way that ensures transparency" is a standard
-- the Commissioner's publication meets or does not: an input flag on the act.
@ref s.57(a) (src:421)
GIVEN `a financial sanction was imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount was reduced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of person` IS A `Person kind`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 55 to 57`
`s 57(a) — the Commissioner must publish the particulars of the financial sanction` `a financial sanction was imposed` `the amount was reduced` `the kind of person` MEANS
    IF   `a financial sanction was imposed`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST  `publish on the Ministry website the particulars of the financial sanction` `the Commissioner` published transparent
               PROVIDED `s 57(a) — the publication deals with each item as the Law requires, given the items` published `and the numbers required` (`s 57(a) — the numbers of the items the Law requires where` `the amount was reduced` `and the violator is` `the kind of person`)
                        ... transparent
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (b): if an appeal was filed under s.56 against a decision to impose a sanction, the Commissioner shall publish, as (a)
-- provides, the filing of the appeal and its results.  The results exist only once the appeal is decided.
-- src:428 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} הוגש ערעור לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 56|סעיף 56}} על החלטת הממונה להטיל עיצום כספי, יפרסם הממונה, לפי סעיף קטן (א), את דבר הגשת הערעור ואת תוצאותיו.
@ref s.57(b) (src:428)
GIVEN `an appeal was filed against the decision to impose a sanction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal has been decided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 55 to 57`
`s 57(b) — the Commissioner must publish the appeal and its result` `an appeal was filed against the decision to impose a sanction` `the appeal has been decided` MEANS
    IF   `an appeal was filed against the decision to impose a sanction`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST  `publish on the Ministry website that an appeal was filed and how it ended` `the Commissioner` filed result
               PROVIDED filed AND ((NOT `the appeal has been decided`) OR result)
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (c): the name of a violator who is an individual MAY be published, after he was given the opportunity to make
-- representations about it, if the Commissioner thinks it necessary to warn the public.  The opportunity may be the s.43
-- representations, provided the notice of intention under s.42 told him of the intention to publish his name.  Item (6)
-- is subject to (d): a name s.9(a) of the Freedom of Information Law bars is not published.
-- src:429 | {{ח:תת|(ג)}} על אף הוראות סעיף קטן (א)(6), הממונה רשאי לפרסם את שמו של מפר שהוא יחיד, לאחר שנתן לו הזדמנות לטעון את טענותיו לעניין זה, אם סבר שהדבר נחוץ לצורך אזהרת הציבור; ההזדמנות לטעון טענות לפי סעיף קטן זה, יכול שתינתן למפר במסגרת זכות הטיעון לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 43|סעיף 43}}, ובלבד שהממונה הודיע למפר על כוונתו לפרסם את שמו, בהודעה על כוונת חיוב לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 42|סעיף 42}}.
@ref s.57(c) (src:429)
GIVEN `the kind of person` IS A `Person kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57(c) — the violator is an individual` `the kind of person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of person`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a corporation` THEN FALSE

@ref s.57(c) (src:429)
GIVEN `the kind of person` IS A `Person kind`
      `the violator was given a separate opportunity to make representations about publication of his name` IS A BOOLEAN
      notice IS A `Notice of intention`
      `the Commissioner thinks publication necessary to warn the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name is barred from disclosure by section 9(a) of the Freedom of Information Law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57(c) — the Commissioner may publish the name of the violator` `the kind of person` `who was given a separate opportunity:` `the violator was given a separate opportunity to make representations about publication of his name` `by the notice of intention` notice `the Commissioner thinking publication necessary to warn the public:` `the Commissioner thinks publication necessary to warn the public` `and the name being barred by section 9(a):` `the name is barred from disclosure by section 9(a) of the Freedom of Information Law` MEANS
        "a violator who is an individual" ... `s 57(c) — the violator is an individual` `the kind of person`
    ... "the opportunity to make representations" ... (`the violator was given a separate opportunity to make representations about publication of his name` OR notice's `states the intention to publish the violator's name`)
    ... "necessary to warn the public" ... `the Commissioner thinks publication necessary to warn the public`
    AND "not barred by section 9(a)" ... NOT `the name is barred from disclosure by section 9(a) of the Freedom of Information Law`

@ref s.57(c) (src:429)
GIVEN `the Commissioner may publish the name of the violator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 55 to 57`
`s 57(c) — the Commissioner's power to publish an individual's name` `the Commissioner may publish the name of the violator` MEANS
    IF   `the Commissioner may publish the name of the violator`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MAY   `publish the name of an individual violator on the Ministry website` `the Commissioner`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (d): the Commissioner SHANT publish a particular that s.9(a) of the Freedom of Information Law bars.  The act is the
-- publication of a particular; the guard picks the forbidden one.
-- src:430 | {{ח:תת|(ד)}} על אף האמור בסעיף זה, לא יפרסם הממונה פרטים שהם בגדר מידע, שרשות ציבורית מנועה מלמסור לפי {{ח:חיצוני|חוק חופש המידע#סעיף 9|סעיף 9(א) לחוק חופש המידע, התשנ״ח–1998}}, וכן רשאי הוא שלא לפרסם פרטים לפי סעיף זה, שהם בגדר מידע שרשות ציבורית אינה חייבת למסור לפי {{ח:חיצוני|חוק חופש המידע#סעיף 9|סעיף 9(ב) לחוק האמור}}.
@ref s.57(d) (src:430)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 55 to 57`
`s 57(d) — the Commissioner shall not publish a particular that section 9(a) bars` MEANS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    SHANT `publish a particular on the Ministry website` `the Commissioner` particular
          PROVIDED particular's `barred from disclosure by section 9(a) of the Freedom of Information Law`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the Commissioner` BECAUSE "s 57(d): the Commissioner published a particular that section 9(a) of the Freedom of Information Law bars a public authority from disclosing"

-- (e): the publication lasts four years for a corporation, two for an individual: P37, kind V.  IL s.10(b), years after
-- the day of publication, and IL s.10(c) NOT applied (ruling 4); the last day is inside the period.
-- src:431 | {{ח:תת|(ה)}} פרסום לפי סעיף זה בעניין עיצום כספי שהוטל על תאגיד יהיה לתקופה של ארבע שנים, ובעניין עיצום כספי שהוטל על יחיד – לתקופה של שנתיים; בפרסום כאמור יישם המשרד אמצעים טכנולוגיים נאותים ומתקדמים כדי למנוע, ככל האפשר, את העיון בפרטים שפורסמו באתר האינטרנט של המשרד בתום תקופת הפרסום, ובלבד שיש אמצעים מקובלים למניעת העיון כאמור.
@ref s.57(e) (src:431)
@export The last day of the period for which a financial sanction stays published on the Ministry website: four years from the day of publication for a corporation, two years for an individual
GIVEN `the day of publication` IS A DATE @desc The day the particulars were published, as an ISO 8601 date
      `the kind of person` IS A `Person kind` @desc Whether the violator is an individual or a corporation
GIVETH A DATE
`s 57(e) — the last day of the publication period that began on` `the day of publication` `for` `the kind of person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of person`
    WHEN `a corporation` THEN `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 4 `years after an event on` `the day of publication`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 2 `years after an event on` `the day of publication`

@ref s.57(e) (src:431)
GIVEN `the day of publication` IS A DATE
      `the kind of person` IS A `Person kind`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 57(e) — with s 10(c) applied, the last day of the publication period that began on` `the day of publication` `for` `the kind of person` `with` calendar MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of person`
    WHEN `a corporation` THEN `s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` 4 `years after an event on` `the day of publication` `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`Chapter 6 — the days of rest, recess or holiday of` calendar)
    WHEN `an individual` THEN `s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` 2 `years after an event on` `the day of publication` `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`Chapter 6 — the days of rest, recess or holiday of` calendar)

-- Is a day inside the publication period?  The first day is the day after publication; the last day is inside.
@ref s.57(e) (src:431)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the day of publication` IS A DATE
      `the kind of person` IS A `Person kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57(e) — the day` day `is within the publication period that began on` `the day of publication` `for` `the kind of person` MEANS
    `s 8, s 10 — the date` day `is inside the period beginning on` (`s 10 — the first day of a period counted from or after an event on` `the day of publication`) `and ending on` (`s 57(e) — the last day of the publication period that began on` `the day of publication` `for` `the kind of person`)

-- "At the end of the publication period the Ministry shall apply suitable and advanced technological measures to
-- prevent, as far as possible, viewing of the particulars on its website, provided there are accepted means of
-- preventing it."  The window opens when the period ends (the day after its last day); an act before then is not
-- performance.  The Ministry is the party the sentence names.
@ref s.57(e) (src:431)
GIVEN `the day of publication` IS A DATE
      `the kind of person` IS A `Person kind`
      `accepted means of preventing viewing exist` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 55 to 57`
`s 57(e) — the Ministry must apply technological measures when the publication that began on` `the day of publication` `for` `the kind of person` `ends, if accepted means exist:` `accepted means of preventing viewing exist` MEANS
    IF   `accepted means of preventing viewing exist`
    THEN PARTY `the Ministry`
         MUST  `apply technological measures against viewing the published particulars` `the Ministry`
         AFTER (Day (`s 10 — the first day of a period counted from or after an event on` (`s 57(e) — the last day of the publication period that began on` `the day of publication` `for` `the kind of person`))) MINUS (Day `the day of publication`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (f): "The Minister may set further ways to publish the particulars stated in this section."  A power of the
-- Minister (ruling 2: encoded as a MAY, typed by who acts and what is done), with no precondition the section
-- states.  Its content, the further ways, is an input and none is in the sources, so no rule here consults it: the
-- ways of publishing that the Law itself states are the Ministry website (s.57(a)) and, for the updated amounts,
-- Reshumot (s.47(c)).
-- src:432 | {{ח:תת|(ו)}} השר רשאי לקבוע דרכים נוספות לפרסום הפרטים האמורים בסעיף זה.
@ref s.57(f) (src:432)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 55 to 57`
`s 57(f) — the Minister may set further ways of publishing the particulars` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY   `set further ways of publishing the particulars` `the Minister`
